{
  "title": "Model Context Protocol (MCP): Connect Tools to Your AI Assistants | CrestApps for Orchard Core",
  "description": "An AI assistant is only as useful as the tools and information it can reach. The CrestApps Model Context Protocol (MCP) features let your Orchard Core assistants use the tools of outside MCP servers, and let your site share its own tools and prompts with other AI apps.\n\nIn this video:\n• Why a common standard for AI tools helps\n• How the MCP client and the MCP server fit together\n• Adding a connection to an MCP server on the web, and to a local program\n• The sign-in options of a connection\n• Giving an assistant the tools of a connection\n• Sharing your site's tools with the MCP Server settings\n• Sharing prompts with other AI apps\n• Use cases",
